  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "gr_h",
   "x": 145,
   "y": 1658,
   "width": 1450,
   "height": 26,
   "text": "GUARDRAILS \u2014 what gate 3 (VERIFY) is actually checking",
   "originalText": "GUARDRAILS \u2014 what gate 3 (VERIFY) is actually checking",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 900004,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 900005,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "gr_b",
   "x": 145,
   "y": 1690,
   "width": 1450,
   "height": 190,
   "text": "A guardrail is a VALIDATION LEVEL declared in your PRD and carried into the plan. Nothing more exotic than that:\nthe commands that must come back green before a phase may commit \u2014 written by a human, before any agent runs.\n\n   the PRD    \u00a7Implementation phases   \u2192 which levels gate THIS phase\n   the plan   ## VALIDATION COMMANDS   \u2192 those levels copied verbatim, with the exact command + pass condition\n   the config [validation] levels      \u2192 the repo's canonical command for each level\n\n\u26d4 The orchestrator never invents a guardrail and never drops one. A level nobody declared is a level nobody runs.\n\nThe e2e gate, the coupling check and the end-of-PRD review are NOT guardrails \u2014 they are the loop's own gates,\nowned by the orchestrator rather than by your PRD, and reported separately. \"Guardrails passed\" means exactly:\nthe validation levels your PRD declared came back green.",
   "originalText": "A guardrail is a VALIDATION LEVEL declared in your PRD and carried into the plan. Nothing more exotic than that:\nthe commands that must come back green before a phase may commit \u2014 written by a human, before any agent runs.\n\n   the PRD    \u00a7Implementation phases   \u2192 which levels gate THIS phase\n   the plan   ## VALIDATION COMMANDS   \u2192 those levels copied verbatim, with the exact command + pass condition\n   the config [validation] levels      \u2192 the repo's canonical command for each level\n\n\u26d4 The orchestrator never invents a guardrail and never drops one. A level nobody declared is a level nobody runs.\n\nThe e2e gate, the coupling check and the end-of-PRD review are NOT guardrails \u2014 they are the loop's own gates,\nowned by the orchestrator rather than by your PRD, and reported separately. \"Guardrails passed\" means exactly:\nthe validation levels your PRD declared came back green.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
